<title>USA: Vermont Teddy Bear Co Q3 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Vermont Teddy Bear Co Q3 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>SHELBURNE, Vt. 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>For period ended March 31</p>
<p>			1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr loss	  $0.14	  profit  $0.06</p>
<p> Net loss	   714	   profit   284</p>
<p> Revs		 5,330		    5,131</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  5,161		    5,161</p>
<p>	   9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss	  $0.24	  loss    $0.06</p>
<p> Net loss	   1,228	 loss     303</p>
<p> Revs		 12,739		   12,858</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  5,161		    5,161</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Notes: company attributed Q1 loss to higher selling expenses and higher operating costs associated with new stores. Company president Pat Burns said, &quot;We simply overreached with certain new marketing initiatives.&quot; The 3.9 percent rise in revenues is the result of new store openings in North Conway, N.H., and New York City.</p>
